        },
        "prob_body": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Every time you check a bag you hand the airline $45 to $50 each way. That is $90 to $100 per round trip, before overweight penalties, before delays, and before the 45 minutes at the carousel you never get back.</p><p>It adds up faster than most people count:</p><ul><li>$50 to $75 in overweight penalties when a case goes over</li><li>$30 to $60 for a carry-on on budget airlines</li><li>26 million bags mishandled every year</li><li>$700 or more a year for a family of four flying twice</li></ul><p>You have tried rolling. You have tried packing cubes. You have tried sitting on the lid. None of it works, because none of it touches the actual problem: your clothes take up more room than your suitcase has.</p>",
            "width": "100%",
            "max_width": "normal",
