    "section_Wy2Bag1": {
      "type": "section",
      "blocks": {
        "text_2bag_head": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h2><strong>Why Two Bags, Not One</strong></h2>",
            "width": "100%",
            "max_width": "normal",
            "alignment": "left",
            "type_preset": "h4",
            "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
            "font_size": "1rem",
            "line_height": "normal",
            "letter_spacing": "normal",
            "case": "none",
            "wrap": "pretty",
            "color": "var(--color-foreground-heading)",
            "background": false,
            "background_color": "#00000026",
            "corner_radius": 0,
            "padding-block-start": 0,
            "padding-block-end": 0,
            "padding-inline-start": 0,
            "padding-inline-end": 0
          },
          "blocks": {},
          "name": "t:names.heading"
        },
        "text_2bag_body": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Every other kit in this category sells you a single bag. The second one is not a bonus, it is the part that makes the system work on a real trip.</p><p><strong>One for clean, one for worn.</strong> Packing falls apart around day three, when yesterday’s clothes go back in with the fresh ones and the whole case starts to smell like the trip. Give the second bag to your laundry. Zipped shut it keeps the odor in, so what is still in the first bag smells like it did when you left.</p><p><strong>Five days, one carry-on, room to spare.</strong> A solo wardrobe for a five-day trip compresses into a single bag and leaves the other one free for the way home. No checked bag, no baggage claim, no fee.</p><p><strong>Or a much lighter trip for the family.</strong> Two bags hold roughly what a full checked bag holds, so one kit takes a serious bite out of what you would otherwise check. For four or five people, plan on two kits: that is what it took on our own last trip, and the quantity selector above is there for exactly that.</p><p><strong>$89.99, once.</strong> One round trip of checked-bag fees runs $90 to $100. The kit clears its own cost on the first trip, and every flight after that is money you keep.</p>",
            "width": "100%",
            "max_width": "none",
            "alignment": "left",
            "type_preset": "rte",
            "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
            "font_size": "",
            "line_height": "normal",
            "letter_spacing": "normal",
            "case": "none",
            "wrap": "pretty",
            "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
            "background": false,
            "background_color": "#00000026",
            "corner_radius": 0,
            "padding-block-start": 0,
            "padding-block-end": 0,
            "padding-inline-start": 0,
            "padding-inline-end": 0
          },
          "blocks": {}
